00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.180
When working with spreadsheets, there
may be occasions where you need to

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:07.320
work with multiple worksheets and have
that data linked across the worksheets.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.120
You also may need to add hyperlinks that
will jump from one specific worksheet

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.770
to another worksheet or even to an
external document or an external website.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:21.030
So using the sample document
that we've been working with

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.860
as you've watched these videos.

00:00:23.505 --> 00:00:26.924
I'm now going to show you how
you can link information from one

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:28.365
work sheet to another worksheet.

00:00:29.085 --> 00:00:32.114
So the first thing I'm going to do is
this one is still called sheet one.

00:00:32.235 --> 00:00:34.125
So what I'm going to do is
I'm going to rename that.

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:38.295
So just double click on it
and I can then delete that.

00:00:38.415 --> 00:00:42.584
And I'm going to call this
the sales data worksheet.

00:00:43.605 --> 00:00:45.705
So that is now the sales data worksheet.

00:00:45.885 --> 00:00:48.185
And I'm going to add another worksheet.

00:00:48.185 --> 00:00:50.640
So if I click on the little
plus sign at the bottom.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.260
That brings up a new worksheet.

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.320
And in this worksheet, I'm just
going to rename it so I can double

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:59.580
click on it to rename it, or I
can right-click and select rename.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:06.450
And I'm just going to call
this one, the average sales.

00:01:08.179 --> 00:01:10.095
So there's no information
on this worksheet yet.

00:01:10.095 --> 00:01:13.304
So I'm going to copy some information
from here, but I'm going to copy it.

00:01:13.664 --> 00:01:16.785
And when I paste it into the new
worksheet, it will be linked to this data.

00:01:17.475 --> 00:01:22.035
So what I want on this new worksheet
is I want basically the first

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.470
columns showing the actual sales, the
monthly sales, not the total sales,

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.920
the total income or the target met.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.580
Just the information that relates
to the products, the price and the

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.050
sales that were from January to
July, including the average sales.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.080
So I have highlighted
all of that information.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.550
So if I now use the shortcut
Control and C, and I've selected

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.310
information, so I've copied that,
and that's now on the clipboard.

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:52.320
If I go to the average sales
worksheet and select cell A1, I

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.300
can go to the paste option there.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:02.100
And then that gives me a range of options,
or I can also right-click in that cell.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.700
And then this gives me
the options for pasting.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:09.390
And what I'm looking for is I'm
looking for the paste link option.

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:14.010
So it's a little clipboard with
a two chain links together, and

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:18.240
I select that, and that has now
pasted that as a linked object.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:24.480
And just to make the data more
presentable I can just do the little

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.109
triangle and double-click between
two of the columns to make sure that

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:29.760
the data is all clear and visible.

00:02:31.619 --> 00:02:35.040
So we'll go back to
that and select escape.

00:02:35.339 --> 00:02:37.470
So I've got the information on there.

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:41.774
And as you can see, it mirrors
the information on the average

00:02:41.774 --> 00:02:43.484
sales so they're both the same.

00:02:43.905 --> 00:02:47.505
And you can tell that it is linked that
if I'm on the average sales and I select

00:02:47.505 --> 00:02:52.005
one of the cells, you can see in the
formula bar that it equals sales data,

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:56.834
C2, so it's equalling, and it's looking
on the sales data worksheet, and it's

00:02:56.834 --> 00:03:06.114
looking at cell C2 and similarly for the
February sales, sales data, D2 and for the

00:03:06.114 --> 00:03:10.684
March sales, for the one hour experience,
sales data E5 and the average sales.

00:03:11.085 --> 00:03:15.075
So again, as you can see, all
of the information is linked

00:03:15.135 --> 00:03:16.545
to the previous worksheet.

00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:19.365
So if anything has changed on here.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:25.575
So for example, I changed the January
sales for the weekend experience.

00:03:26.805 --> 00:03:33.465
And if I look at that now that will
automatically update on the average sales.

00:03:33.465 --> 00:03:39.315
So any data that has changed on here,
but only in that area there, if that

00:03:39.315 --> 00:03:43.305
information changes, obviously we didn't
copy and paste that because we didn't

00:03:43.305 --> 00:03:45.765
want to show that there that won't change.

00:03:46.695 --> 00:03:51.225
So for example, it may be a case that
I need a new worksheet and I'm going

00:03:51.225 --> 00:04:01.415
to click on another worksheet and this
one here, I'm going to call "income".

00:04:06.065 --> 00:04:10.115
And again, there's nothing on there.

00:04:10.655 --> 00:04:15.965
And in this one, I'm just going to
demonstrate how I can link information

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.065
by selecting non-adjacent columns.

00:04:18.095 --> 00:04:22.235
So for the first one, we selected those
columns, which was quite straightforward.

00:04:22.235 --> 00:04:25.505
I just clicked in product, held
the mouse down and dragged it along

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.540
till I had selected the information.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:32.980
For this one I need this
information and this information.

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.910
So I can't do that
straightforward by doing that.

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:41.090
What I have to do is the first
thing I do is I have to select the

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:45.260
information that I require in these
two columns, which is that, and then

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:50.450
hold down the CTRL key and then I can
go along and select the information

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:53.510
that I require in columns J, K and L.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.859
And again, I can now select copy.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.469
So Control and C.

00:04:57.539 --> 00:05:01.080
As you can see, both areas
have been selected and copied.

00:05:01.229 --> 00:05:05.310
If I go to income, I can then
right-click into that cell,

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.590
paste the link option again.

00:05:08.039 --> 00:05:12.359
And as you can see, I'll just widen
the columns a little bit so everything

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:14.549
will be seen, that is still linked.

00:05:15.525 --> 00:05:19.325
So that shows you how you can
link data within worksheets, so

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:24.825
this time if you want to have
information on specific worksheets.

00:05:24.975 --> 00:05:31.335
So again, if I change the April
sales there to that, obviously

00:05:31.335 --> 00:05:34.875
all that information changes,
but it will also change on the

00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:37.865
income as well as the average.

00:05:39.995 --> 00:05:44.595
As well as linking information on
separate worksheets, it may be a case

00:05:44.595 --> 00:05:45.795
that you need to add a hyperlink.

00:05:45.795 --> 00:05:50.025
So I may need to add a hyperlink
that will go to -  straight to the

00:05:50.025 --> 00:05:52.035
income or the average sales worksheet.

00:05:52.065 --> 00:05:56.295
So I can take the text in there, if
I typed in the text average sales,

00:06:01.055 --> 00:06:04.205
and I then right-clicked on that.

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:08.100
I can select link at the very bottom.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.640
So if I select link, it will
then ask me what I want to do.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.830
So this is inserting a hyperlink.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.520
So a hyperlink is the same, whether
it's linking between different

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:21.090
worksheets within a spreadsheet,
or whether you're going to actually

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.320
link to an external source.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:25.440
It just means that you have
to select the right option.

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:28.920
So for this instance, I'm going to
select a place in this document.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:32.650
Now when I select place in this
document, it automatically tells me

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.510
which worksheets that I can link to.

00:06:34.539 --> 00:06:38.440
So I've typed the text, average sales,
and I'm going to link to the average

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:43.870
sales, select OK, and as you can see, it's
now gone blue so it's like a web link.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.560
If I click on that, it automatically
jumps to the average sales.

00:06:47.919 --> 00:06:53.530
So if I click on there and it jumps
to the average sales, and again, if

00:06:53.530 --> 00:07:01.710
I go back and I select income, and
then I right click on that and select

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:07.020
link, place in this document, and I
needed to go to the income worksheet.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:11.130
And then if I open that up and
then click on that, it takes me

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.630
straight to the income worksheet.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:16.320
Obviously we haven't got much data on
the spreadsheet, but if you're working

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:21.600
with multiple worksheets within a
spreadsheet, this can be extremely useful.

00:07:25.965 --> 00:07:29.865
As with Word or PowerPoint, you
may also apply hyperlinks to

00:07:30.045 --> 00:07:32.085
websites or other documents.

00:07:32.565 --> 00:07:36.705
And again, all you would do there
is you would insert some text, so

00:07:36.705 --> 00:07:45.885
it could be home page and you could
then right-click on that, select link

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:50.055
and it would be an existing file or
webpage that you would need to select.

00:07:50.085 --> 00:07:52.935
So if it's in the document, you
would select place in this document,

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.170
or existing file or webpage.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.560
The text to display would be
homepage and then whatever web

00:07:58.560 --> 00:07:59.760
address you wanted to put in.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:10.770
So just as an example, I'll just
type in Google and select OK.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:15.410
And that is now taking me to Google.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:17.200
When I click on that and...

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.255
go back to the spreadsheet.

00:08:23.675 --> 00:08:31.145
So you can add links whether it be
within the workbook or to external sites.

